From e55408678bdd29f564735bea8e4383020f963a2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Constantin Adam <cmadam@us.ibm.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:07:33 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Pass determinism_check="none" to non-reentrant activation
 checkpointing

Non-reentrant checkpoint_wrapper defaults to determinism_check="default",
which compares the tensor metadata recorded in the forward pass with the
metadata produced by the recomputation and raises on any mismatch. Under
mixed precision the recompute can legitimately differ (bf16 forward,
fp32 recompute of the upcast RoPE/attention path), so training aborts in
the first checkpointed block. "none" skips that comparison and keeps the
wrapper non-reentrant, which is what FSDP2 requires.

functools.partial is already imported for the reentrant branch below.

Applied as a runtime sed by gbansible
(roles/lm_engine_pretrain_job/templates/appwrapper_pretrain.yml.j2); baked
here so the image does not depend on the launcher patching its own
source. Not present in the reference image
us.icr.io/cil15-shared-registry/lm-engine:0.1.0-cuda-fa2cc.
---
 lm_engine/training/gradient_checkpointing/block.py | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/lm_engine/training/gradient_checkpointing/block.py b/lm_engine/training/gradient_checkpointing/block.py
index 6039df9..cd73e73 100644
--- a/lm_engine/training/gradient_checkpointing/block.py
+++ b/lm_engine/training/gradient_checkpointing/block.py
@@ -32,7 +32,7 @@ def block_checkpointing(
                 return True
         return False
 
-    checkpoint_wrapper_function = checkpoint_wrapper
+    checkpoint_wrapper_function = partial(checkpoint_wrapper, determinism_check="none")
     if use_reentrant:
         checkpoint_wrapper_function = partial(checkpoint_wrapper, checkpoint_impl=CheckpointImpl.REENTRANT)
 
